  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1226 AM MDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nThursday sees the monsoon high slide over NM bringing hotter \ntemperatures to the area, notably eastern NM where low to mid 100s \nwill be favored again. Highs in the 90s to near 100 will favor lower \nelevation areas of central and western NM. A moderate to high heat \nrisk will result each day, mainly for central and eastern NM as a \nresult. Lingering low-level moisture will favor a moisture recycling \ntrend each day Thursday onward through the weekend with little \nchanges to the overall weather pattern as the high loiters over NM. \nAs such, expect daily rounds of afternoon thunderstorm activity \ndeveloping over the high terrain, slowly meandering over surrounding \nlower elevations late afternoon, and lingering and dying out through \nthe late evening hours. Wetting footprints will be small as such, \nwith localized rain shafts under storms. Any flash flooding concerns \nwill be where the slowest storms occur, but suppression beneath the \nhigh should limit this threat.",
